coder › Done. Implemented both functions in `src/query.ts` and added `src/query.test.ts`.

## What changed

**`src/query.ts`**
- `parseQuery(text)`:
  - Strips one optional leading `?`.
  - Returns `{}` for empty input.
  - Splits on `&`, skipping empty pairs (so `a=1&&b=2&` parses cleanly).
  - Splits each pair on the *first* `=`; no `=` means the value is `''`.
  - Decodes percent-encoding and maps `+` to a space (replacing `+` before `decodeURIComponent`, so a literal `%2B` still decodes to `+`).
  - A key seen once maps to its string value; seen again it becomes (or extends) an array, in order.
- `stringifyQuery(query)`:
  - Iterates keys in insertion order via `Object.entries`.
  - Emits one `key=value` pair per array element.
  - Percent-encodes values with `encodeURIComponent` (spaces become `%20`), and encodes keys the same way so round trips hold for keys with special characters.
  - No leading `?`.

**`src/query.test.ts`** — 15 tests covering each parse rule, stringify rules (order, arrays, `%20` spaces, no leading `?`), and two round trips.

